C3 -- the long march: >= 30 000 accepted sub-steps with sum(Y) inside 4*eps*N
==============================================================================================
  TWO things have to hold at once, and finding a problem where both do is the instrument:

    (1) the march must actually DEMAND 30 000 sub-steps. The limiter is adaptive, so the
        count is roughly (total fractional traversal) / maximumFractionalChange -- it cannot
        be dialled up by asking for a longer dt, because once the chemistry stops changing
        the whole remaining time goes in ONE step. A first attempt at dt = 600 took 59.
    (2) the problem must EXERCISE round-off. A reversible mechanism holds both species at
        O(1) indefinitely; the irreversible one decays to ~1e-323 where every addition is
        exact and the plain march drifts 0.00 eps over 7 521 sub-steps (audit 2.1).

  So the control is swept until the count clears 30 000, on the reversible problem.

